up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 7.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.3, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.3 to 8.4. December accounts for 17% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 18% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 14,800 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar distribution could result from routine planning. Contracts just under the limit may reflect market rates or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check if multiple contracts cover the same need. Review awardee A’s contracts for patterns. Examine contract [1]’s terms to see if it aligns with other contracts in the same category.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["qWNY4uoYxzMtm4eBPtV6eQ%3D%3D","MmzXrNjuXaQS7pcxhTeWOg%3D%3D","9W0%2ByMkk6Xyzz8fXU2i3eQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}